 Job Title: Production Planning and Control Manager 
 About Pratt & Whitney Canada 
 Pratt & Whitney Canada (P&WC) is a global leader in aerospace innovation, proudly headquartered in Longueuil, Quebec, since 1928. We design and manufacture next-generation aircraft engines that power the world’s largest fleet of business, general aviation, and regional aircraft and helicopters.
 For nearly 100 years, our teams have been at the forefront of propulsion technology, pushing boundaries to make flight more efficient and reliable. Our engines support missions that truly matter, from transporting people and essential goods, to enabling emergency medical services, humanitarian operations, and wildfire suppression around the world.
 An Employer of Choice 
 Pratt & Whitney Canada was named one of Canada’s Best Employers for 2026 by Forbes, marking the 11th consecutive year the company has earned this recognition. Pratt & Whitney Canada also ranked #1 employer in the aerospace and defense industry in the country. In addition, our headquarters continues to be recognized among the top employers in the Montreal region. Together, these distinctions reinforce our reputation as an employer of choice in Montreal, across Canada, and around the world.
 Why Join The Team? 
 The CFL (Centre manufacturier Longueuil) organization is looking for a dynamic, creative, and organized individual who is eager to contribute to P&WC’s business objectives through production planning and control. The responsibilities associated with this position are diverse, rewarding, and involve collaboration with various departments across P&WC. If you have strong organizational skills, leadership abilities, initiative, and autonomy, as well as a passion for management, this is an excellent opportunity for you.
 Supported by a strong team and collaborating with various groups and partners across the organization, you will be responsible for leading a production planning team that oversees production planning and control for all CFL activities.
 The position also includes recruiting new team members, as well as providing the development and mentorship required to maintain key competencies. You will be responsible for ensuring that the services provided remain aligned with the company’s strategy in a constantly evolving environment.
 This is a full-time day shift position from Monday to Friday based in Longueuil, and performed exclusively on-site. 
 What your day to day will look like? 
 Collaborate closely with the various Business Unit Managers (MLMs) to implement strategies aimed at meeting customer demand and business objectives;
 Ensure effective production planning across all areas under your responsibility in order to achieve the sector’s business objectives;
 Implement effective routines to maintain the accuracy and quality of all data required for effective production planning;
 Support the production planning team in its interactions with support functions to ensure smooth and efficient operations;
 Maintain and develop a supplier base that meets our quality and efficiency requirements in order to support our manufacturing operations;
 Ensure that the production planning team implements strategies to meet our various KPIs related to inventory management;
 Continue to monitor and deploy the department’s transformation initiatives (CORE) in order to increase the stability and quality of the work performed by the entire production planning team;
